    "Observations from your own history, not medical advice. Talk to a clinician about anything that concerns you.": {},
    "Occasions": {},
    "On your home screen": {},
    "On-device summaries": {},
    "Once there are weigh-ins either side of a dose, this will show what changed and how fast.": {},
    "One card here can be checked today: the blood-pressure estimate. Log a cuff reading after the app has estimated one and the pair is recorded automatically — the app's guess, your measurement, and the date. Five pairs and this can say how far out it typically is.": {},
    "One file, as JSON, containing all of it: every individual reading; the signal inventory (how many readings each signal has, over what dates, from which device); every card as it reads right now, with its drivers and weighted shares; what the cards judge against — your personal baselines and comparison pools; the troubleshooting log; and your corrections, with what the app guessed and what you said. It runs to tens of megabytes on a long history, so it's a file to share rather than something to paste.": {},
    "One instrument each, so nothing to choose between": {},
    "One serving": {},
    "One serving is (optional)": {},
    "Only %lld of the last 7 days recorded any effort, so there is no weekly figure — a total built from one worn day reads as a quiet week when what happened is that the watch was off.": {},
    "Only needed if you'd rather use “Open URLs” than the app's own action — an old shortcut, or something that can only produce a web address. Add `&stepCount=1234` and so on, one per reading. Send the same day twice and the second replaces the first, so re-running to fix a number is safe. **Anything the app learns to track later works through either route without you changing anything.**": {},
    "Only one %@ so far": {},
    "Only the numbers are kept — you chose that in Settings ▸ Body scans. This scan can never be re-measured.": {},
    "Open Shotsy": {},
    "Open day": {},
    "Open iOS Settings": {},
    "Open the %@ developer site": {},
    "Opens this day in full": {},
    "Optional": {},
    "Optional — you can do this now or any time in Settings. Tap a device for a simple, step-by-step guide.": {},
    "Or read it off a screenshot": {},
    "Overnight HRV": {},
    "Ovulation is worked out backwards from your next expected period, not forwards from your last one — the second half of a cycle is the steady one at about %lld days, and the first half is where cycles differ. That is why the ± here comes from how much *your* cycles vary rather than from a textbook.": {},
    "Owed": {},
    "Part": {},
    "Passed": {},
    "Paste this exactly into the provider's “Redirect URI” field.": {},
    "Patterns worth a look": {},
    "Per week": {},
    "Per-source averages": {},
    "Placed by clinical category, not a centile": {},
    "Placing a reading against a population needs somebody to have published one, by age and sex. Nobody has for these — they are mostly signals only wearables measure, and the research hasn't caught up. Comparing them against other people using this app is on the roadmap; nothing here is sent anywhere today.": {},
    "Pre-set to what you wore last time. Clothing is the single biggest reason two scans disagree, so change it only if you really are dressed differently — recording the difference is better than hiding it.": {},
    "Predicted": {},
    "Prefer to skip? Just tap Continue — it can be turned on later from the flagged-moments list, and the app will offer once.": {},
    "Prefer to skip? Just tap Continue.": {},
