    "Saying you were not ill answers the app's guess. It does not remove a day your calendar recorded as illness — change that where it was entered.": {},
    "Scale": {},
    "Scan a Screen Time screenshot": {},
    "Scan it": {},
    "Scan the report": {},
    "Scan with the camera": {},
    "Scan your pathology report, pick a photo, or choose a PDF. Every value on it is read on your device — nothing is uploaded — and you confirm each one before it is kept.": {},
    "Scans can be taken, and a future version can re-measure them from what is kept.": {},
    "Score": {},
    "Score over time": {},
    "Screen Time can't be read by any app — Apple sandboxes it deliberately — so a shortcut is the only way it can reach a health app at all. Calendar load is the other one worth collecting: how many hours of meetings a day is a stress signal nothing else here can see.": {},
    "Screen time": {},
    "Screen time and your sleep": {},
    "Screen time that day (min)": {},
    "Screenshot Settings ▸ Screen Time and pick it here — the Week view works too. The text is read on your device, nothing is uploaded, and everything lands for you to check before saving. A daily *average* is never taken as a day's total.": {},
    "Search your data": {},
    "See exactly what would ever leave your phone to make the models better — including your corrections, which are shared in two tiers, both on by default and each switchable off. Nothing is sent in this build. Body scans covers what a scan collects and, separately, what it keeps. Delete everything removes every record on this phone and says plainly what it cannot reach.": {},
