    "Settings": {},
    "Settled": {},
    "Settled means the first point at or below a tenth of the way back up from the night's floor to where it started. A night that never came down has no settling point, and this says so rather than calling it instant.": {},
    "Severity": {},
    "Sex": {},
    "Shaded bands are the systolic categories. The two numbers don't share thresholds — 85 is stage 1 diastolic but normal systolic — so the diastolic limits (80, 90, 120) are the thin dashed lines.": {},
    "Share anonymous accuracy data": {},
    "Share export": {},
